  <prompt>
    Perform ONE consolidated schema pass on the `sprk_communication` Dataverse table so every downstream R4 wave has its landing columns. Add the R3 reply-thread columns and the R4 association columns, confirm two columns already exist, and bring `docs/data-model/sprk_communication.md` up to date (closing the §1.2 doc drift called out in FR-01).

    Add (if missing):
    - `sprk_inreplyto` — Single Line of Text, max length 255, indexed (`isSearchable=true`) — holds the parent message's `Internet-Message-Id` for reply-thread continuity matching by the Association Engine (W1 rung 1).
    - `sprk_internetmessageid` — Single Line of Text, max length 255, indexed — the message's own RFC-2822 `Internet-Message-Id`, stamped post-send (W0 task 006) and read on inbound thread matching.
    - `sprk_associationprovenance` — Multiple Lines of Text (memo), stores the per-attribute confidence + rung + match-reason JSON the Association Engine records per match (W1).
    - `sprk_regardingservicerequest` — Lookup targeting `sprk_servicerequest` — the eighth association target (see task 003 for the doc + wiring half).

    Confirm already-present (do NOT recreate): `sprk_receiveddate` and `sprk_associationstatus`.

    Use the `dataverse-create-schema` skill (Web API + PowerShell — PAC CLI cannot create columns). Verify current state first via Dataverse MCP `describe`; only add what is missing. Update `docs/data-model/sprk_communication.md` regardless of whether any column was added.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Spaarke Dataverse engineer. Authoritative on `sprk_communication` schema. Fluent in the `dataverse-create-schema` skill (Web API column creation, idempotency check) and `docs/data-model/` documentation conventions.
  </role>

  <goal>
    All four columns (`sprk_inreplyto`, `sprk_internetmessageid`, `sprk_associationprovenance`, `sprk_regardingservicerequest`) exist on `sprk_communication` in the dev environment with the correct types; `sprk_receiveddate` + `sprk_associationstatus` confirmed present; `docs/data-model/sprk_communication.md` documents the full current schema (closing §1.2 drift). Owning solution exports cleanly if any column was added.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      R4 collapses the R3 reply-thread schema work and the R4 association work into a single schema pass to avoid multiple solution churn rounds. `sprk_communication` predates this project (R2 server foundation) and has partial coverage: `sprk_associationstatus` + `sprk_receiveddate` land, but the reply-thread and provenance columns and the service-request lookup do not. FR-01 requires closing this and updating the data-model doc, whose §1.2 currently drifts from the live schema.

      Downstream dependents: task 006 (send-path) stamps `sprk_internetmessageid` + `sprk_inreplyto`; task 011 (Association Engine) reads all four; task 015 (confidence→status) writes `sprk_associationstatus` + `sprk_associationprovenance`; task 042 (review surface) reads provenance + the service-request lookup.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>docs/data-model/sprk_communication.md</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/IncomingAssociationResolver.cs</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/CommunicationService.cs</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">Reply-thread + provenance + service-request columns land in ONE schema pass (FR-01) — do not defer any to a later wave.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">`sprk_internetmessageid` and `sprk_inreplyto` MUST be Single Line of Text, max length 255, AND indexed (`isSearchable=true`) — the engine queries them on every inbound message.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">`sprk_associationprovenance` MUST be Multiple Lines of Text (memo) — it holds JSON, not a scalar.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">`sprk_regardingservicerequest` MUST be a Lookup targeting `sprk_servicerequest`. Task 003 authors the doc + `RegardingLookupMap`/priority wiring; this task only creates the column.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">If a column already exists, verify + document only — do NOT recreate. The `dataverse-create-schema` idempotency check covers this. If a column exists with the WRONG type/length/index, STOP and escalate (destructive edits not authorized here).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-024">The Association Engine keeps writing ADR-024 typed regarding lookups + denormalized fields; `sprk_regardingservicerequest` is an additive ADR-024-family lookup, not a new mechanism.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-045">Task 005 authors the Communication ADR; confirm this schema aligns with the association-column contract it codifies (this task may run before 005 lands — no hard dependency, but cite it in the doc update).</constraint>
  </constraints>

