  <steps>
    <step order="1">Read `.claude/skills/dataverse-create-schema/SKILL.md` for the column-creation + idempotency conventions.</step>
    <step order="2">Read `docs/data-model/sprk_communication.md` — capture current documented schema + locate the §1.2 drift.</step>
    <step order="3">Verify live schema via Dataverse MCP `describe` on `sprk_communication`. Record which of the four target columns exist + their shapes; confirm `sprk_receiveddate` + `sprk_associationstatus` present.</step>
    <step order="4">For each missing column, invoke `dataverse-create-schema`: `sprk_inreplyto` (String 255, indexed), `sprk_internetmessageid` (String 255, indexed), `sprk_associationprovenance` (Memo), `sprk_regardingservicerequest` (Lookup → `sprk_servicerequest`). If any exists with the wrong shape → STOP + escalate with the evidence.</step>
    <step order="5">Re-verify all six columns via Dataverse MCP `describe` — confirm final shapes.</step>
    <step order="6">Update `docs/data-model/sprk_communication.md`: document all four added/confirmed columns (logical name, type, length/target, purpose, consumers) and close the §1.2 drift so the doc matches the live schema. Note that `sprk_regardingservicerequest` wiring lands in task 003.</step>
    <step order="7">If any column was added, export the owning solution (`pac solution list` to confirm which solution owns `sprk_communication` schema) so downstream environments pick up the change.</step>
    <step order="8">Update `tasks/TASK-INDEX.md`: mark task 001 ✅; confirm dependents 006/011/015/042 unblocked.</step>
    <step order="9">Update `current-task.md` per task-execute: status → completed; advance to next pending task; record any schema additions in Decisions Made.</step>
  </steps>

