  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    This is the single schema pass that blocks the bulk of R4 (006/011/015/042). Do NOT split it across waves.

    `sprk_inreplyto` is text (holds the parent `Internet-Message-Id` string), NOT a self-referencing lookup — this differs from the R3 task 004 draft, which modeled it as a lookup. R4 uses the RFC-2822 message-id string so the engine can match inbound replies against outbound records without a resolved parent GUID.

    The `sprk_regardingservicerequest` column is created here; its `RegardingLookupMap` + `RegardingFieldPriority` + `TODO_REGARDING_CATALOG` wiring + schema doc land in task 003 (depends on 001).

    If any column exists with the wrong shape, do NOT silently "fix" it — escalate with current-vs-required evidence and pause.
  </notes>

